The fund management application contains multiple security vulnerabilities in its payment handling logic.

### Vulnerability: Unchecked Close Remainder To
### Explanation: The distribute_funds function authorizes payment transactions but fails to validate Txn.close_remainder_to(), allowing an attacker to drain the entire account balance when making a payment.
### Risk: Critical - Complete loss of all funds in the account

### Vulnerability: Unchecked Rekey To
### Explanation: The distribute_funds function authorizes payment transactions but fails to validate Txn.rekey_to(), allowing an attacker to rekey the account to their own address and gain permanent control.
### Risk: Critical - Permanent account takeover

### Vulnerability: Unchecked Payment Receiver
### Explanation: The distribute_funds function authorizes payment transactions but fails to validate Txn.receiver(), allowing an attacker to redirect funds to any arbitrary address instead of the intended recipient.
### Risk: Critical - Complete loss of specified payment amount
